# Python (agentic)

## Types & structure
- Annotate public functions and module boundaries; prefer `from __future__ import annotations`.
- Keep CLI entry thin; put logic in importable modules.
- Prefer pathlib over string path concat.

## Env
- Isolate deps (`venv` / project env); never commit `.env` or tokens.
- Read config from env/settings files already used by the repo — do not invent a second settings tree.

## Async
- Use async for I/O-bound automation/agents/HTTP when the codebase already does; do not convert sync CLI monoliths without need.
- Never block the event loop with long sync work without an executor.

## Agents
- Prefer evidence (exit code, JSON artifact) before claiming success.
- Do not fight repo-specific Python rules (hub `python-hub.mdc`, SaaS rules) — those win on conflict.
